 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "menachot.107a.7",
   "daf": "107a",
   "sentenceId": 6,
   "he": "בַּרְזֶל, תַּנְיָא, אֲחֵרִים אוֹמְרִים: לֹא יִפְחוֹת מִכָּלְיָה עוֹרֵב, וְכַמָּה? אָמַר רַב יוֹסֵף: אַמָּה עַל אַמָּה.",
   "en": "The mishna discusses pledges of gold, silver, and copper. What is the halakha if one says: It is incumbent upon me to donate «iron? It is taught» in a baraita that «others say:» He «must» donate «no less than» the amount that can be made into a base and spike designed to «eliminate the ravens [mikkalya orev].» The Gemara asks: «And how much» is that? «Rav Yosef said:» One «cubit» in width «by» one «cubit» in length."
  },
  {
   "id": "menachot.107a.8",
   "daf": "107a",
   "sentenceId": 7,
   "he": "אִיכָּא דְאָמְרִי: לֹא יִפְחוֹת מֵאַמָּה עַל אַמָּה. לְמַאי חַזְיָא? אָמַר רַב יוֹסֵף: לְכָלְיָה עוֹרֵב.",
   "en": "«There are» those «who say» another version of this baraita and the subsequent explanation: One who pledges to donate iron «must» donate «no less than» one «cubit» in width «by» one «cubit» in length. The Gemara asks: «For what is» this amount of iron «suitable? Rav Yosef said:» It is suitable «for» a base and spike designed to «eliminate the ravens.»"
  }
 ],
